happy Halloween hey guys i'm abby sharp  welcome to Abby's kitchen it is almost  one of my favorite holidays of the whole  year Halloween because let's be real  it's all about the candy and a chocolate  bar thinking back to my childhood during  Halloween when my sister and I used to  go out trick-or-treating  I would always sneak into a room when  she was unsuspecting sneak out all of my  favorite chocolate bars and like replace  them with like the tootsie rolls or like  the lollipops already the crap that  nobody really cares about or wants and  my go-to was definitely those mini  Snickers bars those are one of my  favorite chocolate bars of all time I  love the combination of nugget and  peanuts caramel and of course chocolate  so today I want to share with you a  healthier version these are my vegan  gluten-free no refined sugar added  Snickers bars they are so addictive that  you're definitely not gonna wanna just  wait till Halloween you're gonna want to  make these all year long so let's do  this to make the nougat I add some  almond flour peanut butter maple syrup  Winfrey oat flour and some coconut oil  to a food processor and I process that  until it gets really smooth  then to my baking dish I add some  parchment paper  and then I pack the Nugget into the  bottom of the baking dish  transfer that's the freezer to let it  set up for about ten minutes then to a  saucepot I add some medjool dates the  maple syrup and some coconut cream and I  simmer that on a medium low heat until  it all comes together  then transfer the dates to my food  processor and puree until super smooth  next I mix my date mixture some  chopped-up peanuts I give it a good stir  until it all comes together now it's  time to assemble my frozen nugget I add  my date caramel with peanuts and I  smooth it out and I transfer that to the  freezer for about an hour to set up and  now it's time for some chocolate I cut  my slab into some rectangular bars and  then carefully dip it into some melted  chocolate that I melted in the microwave  with just a little bit of coconut oil  [Music]  let it set on a piece of parchment paper  and joy  so guys I hope you enjoyed this video if  you did be sure to give it the thumbs up  leave me a comment below with what kind  of candy bar you are going to be  stealing from your kids candy bags  subscribe to the channel and I'll see  you next time on Abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

